# kotlin base64 as declarative bindings over java.util.Base64, one host expression an op: the base64 shim's own
# calls (decision 132 of term/self-host/change/001). Malformed input raises IllegalArgumentException, as the shim did.
# Internal: reached only through the public base64 API.

bind to-base64
  take input, like text
  like text
  case kotlin
    text <java.util.Base64.getEncoder().encodeToString(($input).toByteArray(Charsets.UTF_8))>

bind from-base64
  take input, like text
  like text
  case kotlin
    text <String(java.util.Base64.getDecoder().decode($input), Charsets.UTF_8)>
